00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.060
- [Michael] He's most comfortable

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.030
when he's bossing Evan around
and asserting his dominance.

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:13.740
But we see his domineering nature

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:15.660
is motivated by insecurity.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:17.550
He's also brittle and jealous,

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:19.470
afraid of losing his power over Evan

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.000
as they transition into college.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.470
- And I gotta look over at that.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:24.960
Looks like the most fun I've
ever seen in my entire life.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:27.300
- [Michael] Like most
cocky and brash teen boys,

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:29.160
all this attempted
dominance is, of course,

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.920
just a sign of his deep insecurity.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:33.360
- So you're coming to
my party tonight, right?

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:34.530
'Cause it's, like, fully on.

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:35.940
- Yeah, why? Should I not come?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:37.950
- [Michael] This manifests in his intense,

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:41.040
irrational dislike for
Evan's crush, Becca.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:41.873
- Becca's a (beep).

00:11:41.873 --> 00:11:43.590
- [Michael] It's also
visible in Seth's dismay

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.350
that Evan is going to room with Fogell.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:49.164
- I didn't expect this from you, Evan.

00:11:49.164 --> 00:11:50.310
Not from you.

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.560
Gimme that booze, (beep).

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.110
- We never should've had
to hide our arrangement.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.690
- [Michael] While
functionally ruling over Evan,

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:03.270
he's also terrified of
being abandoned by him.

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:05.550
- No, I can't, I gotta
go meet my counselor.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:07.493
I'm picking out my classes for next year.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.410
- What, so I gotta sit
here and eat dessert alone

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.240
like I'm (beep) Steven Glanzberg?

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:14.070
- This suggests he needs Evan's deference

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:16.590
to feel fully recognized
in his own consciousness,

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:19.050
and if Evan fails to show that deference

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:21.300
or even just pay him enough attention,

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:25.650
Seth on some level knows he'll
lose all of his power and,

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:29.220
more importantly, all of
his value as an individual.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.790
So how would Hegel resolve
this unstable relationship?

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:33.960
That is to say,

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:37.110
how would he reconcile
the Seth-Evan dialectic?

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.930
For Hegel, the submissive
member of the pair needs

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:42.690
to acquire an object which
it can express itself

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.160
in relation towards.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:46.650
It's like how, when
your name is Seth Rogen

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:49.080
and you make a gorgeous
ashtray out of clay

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.120
for the 73 joints you smoke each day,

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.610
you can see some of your
consciousness manifested

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:56.670
in its trippy patterns, and
thus you become more aware

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:59.940
of your material ability
to impact the world.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.880
Any time Rogen doubts his own
abilities, he can simply look

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.880
at all of the weed-consuming
accessories he's created

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:08.760
and think, "Wow, Seth,
you really did all this!"

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:12.150
Also, this third thing
mediates the relationship

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:14.730
between the dominant and
the submissive partners

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.200
and makes it so that they're no longer

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:18.270
completely dependent on one another.

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:21.750
And there is something of
this in "Superbad" as well.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.190
Though they're still just kids

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:26.520
who can't really materially
impact the world around them,

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:28.890
they do indeed discover some third thing

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.660
to mediate their relationship through:

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:33.870
their fledgling romances
with Becca and Jules,

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.610
who we must say are of course

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:38.070
also individual self-consciousnesses

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:40.950
and ones that might seem to be even more

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:43.830
dialectically developed
than Seth and Evan.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.960
Seth and Evan's struggle to get booze,

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:48.270
which leads them to crash an adult party

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:51.570
and do minor parkour and major a capella

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:52.770
while running from the cops,

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:55.860
is ultimately their quest to
actualize that third thing

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:58.380
via each one's romantic relationship,

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:01.020
and they spend the whole film
striving to achieve that.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:04.830
Eventually, by entering this
romance, Evan comes to realize

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:07.500
that he is an independent actor from Seth.

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:10.170
By establishing these meaningful
relationships with others,

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:11.790
Evan and Seth are not only able

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:14.190
to be less puppishly
dependent on one another

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:16.140
but also to fully acknowledge

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:19.170
their very real love and friendship.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:20.003
- I love you.

00:14:21.982 --> 00:14:22.923
I love you, man.

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:27.177
- I love you.

00:14:27.177 --> 00:14:29.790
- And key to leaving their
puppy-dog behavior behind

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:31.170
is that they have recognized

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:33.270
their dependence upon each other.

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:34.920
They recognize each other's consciousness

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:37.260
and how that consciousness is essential

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:39.390
to their own sense of self.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:40.980
This is where Hegel's dialectic

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:43.740
can also be seen as a classical example

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:46.470
of the philosophical
concept of recognition,

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:49.980
that is, the idea that
we only become who we are

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:53.310
by being recognized as
such by those around us,

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:55.560
like through our relationships with others

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:57.540
and what we do in the world.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.700
Having been fully
recognized by one another

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:02.250
for who they really are,
Seth and Evan are now ready

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:05.370
to go off to college as
independent young men.

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:07.290
They have been liberated
from their codependence

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:09.060
through their relationships with women.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:11.550
Their friendship is now
no longer characterized

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:14.130
by necessity, but by freedom.

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:16.740
This means they are able to
want what's best for one another

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.020
and no longer seek to hold each other back

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:22.650
out of fear of losing an
essential part of themselves.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:25.860
So already, we can see that
there's some genuine depth

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.050
to the way friendship is
portrayed in "Superbad."

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:29.340
But you're probably wondering:

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:33.180
Did we forget about Fogell
AKA McLovin's wild adventures

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:35.910
with the world's most incompetent cops?

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.050
Absolutely not.

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:39.240
And to understand his absurd storyline,

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:41.640
we need to return to
the idea of recognition,

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:45.540
a concept that Hegel
did not himself invent.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:48.060
That credit is usually given
to his immediate predecessor,

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:51.120
J.G. Fichte, who Hegel
was directly responding to

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:52.650
in "The Phenomenology of Spirit."

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:54.240
Fichte's understanding of recognition

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:56.370
is pretty similar to Hegel's.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.590
He also thinks that we become who we are

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:01.380
by being recognized as such by others.

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.240
But there's one key difference.

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:06.210
Hegel, as we have seen, thinks
that recognition is something

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:09.150
that can only be established
through a struggle,

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.250
but Fiche thinks the
process of recognition

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:13.890
is actually much more automatic.

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:16.050
For Fichte, one comes to be recognized

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:18.810
as an independent, autonomous individual

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:23.130
by being issued a summons from
another free, rational being.

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:25.110
Essentially, the summons is a command

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.720
which says, "You're
free, now act like it."

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.430
It's like how when you're a little kid,

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.590
your parents empower you
to act like a human being

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:34.080
by teaching you how
to, say, tie your shoes

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:36.660
and then expecting you
to do it on a daily basis

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:38.280
or switch to Velcro.

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:40.380
Over time, they'll likely summon you

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:43.560
to take on just about every
responsibility of adulthood

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.900
except probably paying
your own cell phone bill.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:46.920
Thanks, Mom!

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:48.930
And if you ever kick
me off the family plan,

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:51.880
I swear to God you'll never see me again.

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:53.280
Fichte at one point even refers

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:56.730
to this process of summons
as equivalent to upbringing

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:59.730
or to the raising of a
child through community,

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:01.020
and he thinks that this summons

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.630
to be free is bound to
be issued to anyone,

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:06.330
just so long as they have a human body,

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:07.740
which brings us back to Fogell,

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:10.800
who experiences this Fichtean
style of recognition.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.960
When the cops first see
Fogell in the liquor store,

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:15.180
they know his ID is a fake.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:18.390
They know that McLovin
is the unconvincing alias

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:20.400
of a nerdy suburban kid who wants

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:22.890
to be a smooth, womanizing player.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:24.903
- We know you're not 25, man.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:27.990
We're not idiots, McLovin.
- Yeah.

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:29.130
- Did you know the whole time?

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:30.060
- [Michael] But they proceed

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:33.300
as if Fogell was who he
wants to be regardless.

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:35.070
They summon him to be a chill adult

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:38.070
shooting the (beep) with his
grossly negligent cop buddies.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:40.800
And the extraordinary
thing about it is it works.

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:42.823
By being treated as if he was

00:17:42.823 --> 00:17:45.900
a 25-year-old Hawaiian organ
donor with an air of danger

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.960
and a way with the ladies,
Fogell starts to act like it.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.150
After being summoned by these goober cops,

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:53.430
he visibly gains confidence.

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:56.280
He even manages to hook up with a girl,

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:59.760
one who he had previously
struggled to even talk to.

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:04.353
- Uh, it's 10:33. (stammers)

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:06.480
- What?

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:08.670
- [Michael] In this way,
Fogell too experiences

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:11.190
an important sort of an
initiation into adulthood,

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:13.800
learning lessons that he
can use going forward.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:16.380
That's even after the cops
reveal the inauthenticity

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:18.300
behind the whole night when they admit

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:20.700
they knew he was just a regular kid.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.550
You can kinda see a Fichtean
style of recognition then

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:26.490
as the philosophy of "fake
it 'til you make it."

00:18:26.490 --> 00:18:28.440
Notably, we learn that
Fogell's cop buddies

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:31.920
are also striving for their
own kind of recognition,

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:35.100
specifically, to be seen as cool cops.

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:37.700
- You know, cops can have
a fun time, too, you know?

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:42.840
- You know, in a way, I think
we wanted to show ourselves.

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.880
- So I guess you never really age out

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:47.760
of needing some good
old-fashioned recognition, huh?

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:50.010
And thanks in advance to
all the hip 21-year-olds

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:53.760
who don't ask me whose dad
I am when I'm at concerts.

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:56.280
It means a lot to my fragile geist.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:59.040
So clearly Fichte's account
of recognition helps us

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:02.130
make sense of McLovin's wild ride.

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:03.510
But the question remains:

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:05.700
Which style of recognition
is more effective

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:08.610
in understanding the
development of consciousness,

00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:10.470
Fichte's or Hegel's?

00:19:10.470 --> 00:19:14.010
And to that end, is Fogell's
coming-of-age experience

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:16.650
as effective as Evan and Seth's?

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:18.960
Well, obviously Hegel was biased,

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:21.540
but he thought something was
missing from Fichte's account,

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:24.600
that is, the whole
struggle part you undergo

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:26.280
to achieve true recognition.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:28.740
It's kinda like saying that
you can technically do sex

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:30.780
to yourself but it's probably going

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:32.820
to be a more fulfilling
experience if you do sex

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:36.840
with another freely willing
human consciousness.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:38.010
See, through their struggle

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:39.930
to reconcile one another's consciousness,

00:19:39.930 --> 00:19:44.070
Evan and Seth end the film as
serious, independent people.

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:47.670
Fogell, on the other hand, ends
it by destroying a cop car.

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:51.420
He is initiated into a
version of adulthood, sure.

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:53.760
Still, he seems imprisoned in a way

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:56.370
by the limitations of
his role models, who are,

00:19:56.370 --> 00:20:00.243
by their admission, really
not good role models at all.

00:20:02.113 --> 00:20:04.080
- [Michaels] He's not usually
this drunk when he does this,

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:06.600
but I think that could make it more cool.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:07.620
- [Michael] Fogell doesn't go through

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:09.810
any dialectical struggle that teaches him

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.580
to become an independent person.

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:15.270
Instead, he morphs into a
ridiculous fantasy figure:

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:16.590
McLovin.
- Tight.

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:20.190
- If you're recognized for a
fantasy version of yourself,

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:22.710
are you really being recognized at all?

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:25.620
Hegel would probably say, "Nah, bro."

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:27.900
But, like, in German, obviously.

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:31.177
So in short, far from
being just silly, dumb fun,

00:20:31.177 --> 00:20:34.260
"Superbad" starts to look
like an actually deep film

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:36.780
that manages to stage one of
the most important debates

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:38.850
in the history of German idealism

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:41.790
while averaging approximately
two dick jokes a minute.

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:43.320
- They literally made me stop eating foods

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:44.310
that were shaped like dicks.

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:45.930
No hot dogs. No Popsicles.

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.490
Do you know how many foods
are shaped like dicks?

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:49.110
The best kinds.

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:51.453
- By juxtaposing the
stories of Evan and Seth

00:20:51.453 --> 00:20:52.807
and Fogell and McLovin,

00:20:52.807 --> 00:20:55.410
"Superbad" actually shows
us why Hegel's account

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:58.962
of recognition might be
superior to Fichte's.

00:20:58.962 --> 00:21:01.260
In this way, we see that we all could use

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:03.630
a little dialectical struggle of our own

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:06.627
to grow into truly
independent, conscious people.

00:21:06.627 --> 00:21:07.650
But what do you think?

00:21:07.650 --> 00:21:09.540
Is "Superbad" a successful illustration

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:11.430
of a tricky philosophical topic,

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:13.650
are its competing
coming-of-age narratives enough

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:17.250
to make it deep despite all
the talk about bodily fluids,

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:20.220
and is Hegel really
better than Fichte anyway?

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:21.930
Let us know in the comments.

00:21:21.930 --> 00:21:25.890
Big thanks to our patrons for
recognizing our consciousness,

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:27.960
and be sure to check out
all the cool new perks

00:21:27.960 --> 00:21:29.910
on our revamped Patreon page.

